. * Tutorial 1: A first ERGM
. * Requires the core nwcommands and the nwergm package:
. *   net install nwergm, from(https://raw.githubusercontent.com/thomas-u-grund/nwergm/main/)
. 
. nwergm version
nwergm version 1.6.0, 13nov2026
  core package nwcommands : installed (development copy, no distribution date)
  native plugin           : .../nwergm/lib/plugins/macos/ergm_mcmc_macos.plugin (ships with the package, no separate version number)
  compared with           : R ergm 4.12.0
  license                 : GNU GPL-3

. 
. nwwebuse florentine, nwclear

. 
. * The simplest possible ERGM: just an edges term
. nwergm flomarriage, edges

Exponential-family random graph model

Network:               =  flomarriage
Nodes:                 =  16
Ties:                  =  20
Directed:              =  No
Estimation:            =  MPLE

------------------------------------------------------------------------------
 flomarriage | Coefficient  Std. err.      z    P>|z|     [95% conf. interval]
-------------+----------------------------------------------------------------
       edges |  -1.609438    .244949    -6.57   0.000    -2.089529   -1.129347
------------------------------------------------------------------------------

Maximum pseudolikelihood estimate; this is the maximum likelihood estimate only if the model is dyad-independent.

             Null Deviance:     166.4  on 120 degrees of freedom
         Residual Deviance:     108.1  on 119 degrees of freedom

Log-likelihood:   -54.0673 (df = 1)   AIC:     110.1   BIC:     112.9

. 
. * Adding a covariate: does wealth make a marriage tie more likely?
. nwergm flomarriage, edges nodecov(wealth)

Exponential-family random graph model

Network:               =  flomarriage
Nodes:                 =  16
Ties:                  =  20
Directed:              =  No
Estimation:            =  MPLE

--------------------------------------------------------------------------------
   flomarriage | Coefficient  Std. err.      z    P>|z|     [95% conf. interval]
---------------+----------------------------------------------------------------
         edges |  -2.594929   .5360561    -4.84   0.000     -3.64558   -1.544278
nodecov_wealth |   .0105459   .0046743     2.26   0.024     .0013845    .0197073
--------------------------------------------------------------------------------

Maximum pseudolikelihood estimate; this is the maximum likelihood estimate only if the model is dyad-independent.

             Null Deviance:     166.4  on 120 degrees of freedom
         Residual Deviance:     103.1  on 118 degrees of freedom

Log-likelihood:   -51.5543 (df = 2)   AIC:     107.1   BIC:     112.7

. 
. * Information criteria and prediction
. estat ic

Akaike's information criterion and Bayesian information criterion

-----------------------------------------------------------------------------
       Model |        N     ll(null)    ll(model)    df       AIC       BIC
-------------+---------------------------------------------------------------
 flomarriage |      120      -83.178      -51.554     2    107.11    112.68
-----------------------------------------------------------------------------
Note: BIC uses N = number of informative dyads.

. 
. * A dyad-dependent term (triadic closure) is fitted by MCMC
. nwergm flomarriage, edges gwesp(.5) seed(1)

Exponential-family random graph model

Network:               =  flomarriage
Nodes:                 =  16
Ties:                  =  20
Directed:              =  No
Estimation:            =  MCMLE
MCMC sample size:      =  243

------------------------------------------------------------------------------
 flomarriage | Coefficient  Std. err.      z    P>|z|     [95% conf. interval]
-------------+----------------------------------------------------------------
       edges |  -1.690738   .3545529    -4.77   0.000    -2.385649   -.9958271
    gwesp_.5 |   .0917401   .2463391     0.37   0.710    -.3910756    .5745558
------------------------------------------------------------------------------

MCMLE converged after 1 iteration(s).
Evaluating log-likelihood at the estimate (bridge sampling with 16 bridges) ...

             Null Deviance:     166.4  on 120 degrees of freedom
         Residual Deviance:     108.0  on 118 degrees of freedom

Log-likelihood:   -53.9960 (df = 2)   AIC:     112.0   BIC:     117.6
Monte Carlo standard error of the log-likelihood:  .01277

. 
